{"kind":"assert","text":"The Grow demo cannot be packed from current source, and that blocks the release you plan to sign (a5d65e58 item 6) as well as four cutover tests.\n\nFinding, at cutover head 2697c4ff with 94203a73: prepareApplicationDirectory(prepareGrowDemo(), fixedSigner(254)) refuses with ApplicationPackageValidationError. The refused definition is demoSite sha256:7ca60d1e, which is F's pin. Row receives.room-summary fails check endpoint-binding, reason wrong-peer: \"The handler must name and pin the connected sender's definition.\" demo-definitions.ts:75-77 points the Site's create-room send at demoRoom (3ea5dcac). The Site's room-summary receiver still pins the maintained Room 2fc33678. F ruling point 7 named this gap and left it for a separate filing. Main never packs the demo from source. Main's tests read the committed signed bytes (maintained-applications-child.ts:24), and prepareGrowDemo runs only from its own CLI (prepare-demo.ts:36-38). So no test on main exercises the gap.\n\nEffect: no package built from current demo source passes the package-graph check. The release you sign from canonical source fails the same way.\n\nThe four scenarios in archive-installed (production, activation warm, activation evicted, Room A shape) cannot move to the maintained grow. They install with the demo genesis fields sensors, climate and operator (:268, demo-definitions.ts:16-26). They use the demo agent role (:267, prepare-demo.ts:22-26), demo parties (:346) and the agent actions grow.climate and grow.sense (:348). The maintained grow has none of these. Only the device-command, owner-answer and Room A fan parts carry over. The scenarios exist to witness the production archive policy with the demo principals.\n\nOptions:\n(a) Repair demoSite in this head: its room-summary receiver pins demoRoom. demoSite gets a new digest in place of F's pin 7ca60d1e. You rule the new pin, and the note lists it with the other vectors. With e4b72290 question 1 granted, the four scenarios then install a demo built from source and keep their acceptance case. Your signed release builds from the same source.\n(b) Retire the four scenarios with note rows. The demo repair goes to its own request, and your release waits on it.\n(c) Move the scenarios to the maintained grow and keep only the device-command, owner-answer and fan parts. They lose the demo-principal case.\n\nI recommend (a). The gap is a real defect, because the receiver rejects the Room the Site creates. Your release needs the repair either way. And (a) is the one option that keeps the acceptance case. If you choose (a), the worker reports the new demoSite digest, and any other digest that changes, before it commits the pin."}